hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3182","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: Allah's curse to be on the Jews, they made the graves of their Prophets mosques. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3227)"
"3183","narrates regarding the martyrs of Uhud: Some people moved their martyrs from there, so a proclaimer from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) made this announcement: Return the martyrs to the place where they were killed."
"3184","I were not leaving behind daughters after me, I would have liked that you be martyred before me. (Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) says): So I stayed in Madinah Munawwarah. Meanwhile, my paternal aunt’s son brought the bodies of my father and my maternal uncle, carrying them on a camel. He brought them to Madinah Munawwarah so that he could bury both of them in our graveyard. At that moment, a man announced: Beware! Indeed, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) is commanding you to take the slain back and bury them in the field at the very place where they were martyred. The narrator says: So we laid both of them down with the slain at the very place where they were martyred. (Imam Ibn Hibban (may Allah have mercy on him) says:): The words of the narration, “we brought both of them back,” mean that we buried them there."
"3185","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Whoever is wounded in the way of Allah, when he comes on the Day of Resurrection, his blood will be flowing, its color will be like the color of blood and its fragrance will be like the fragrance of musk, and whoever is wounded in the way of Allah, the seal of the martyrs will be placed upon him.”"
"3186","Whom do you consider to be a martyr among you? They (the Companions) said: Messenger, of Allah, one who is slain in the way of Allah is a martyr. He said: Then (if this is the definition of a martyr) the martyrs of my Umma will be small in number. They asked: Messenger of Allah, who are they? He said: One who is slain in the way of Allah is a martyr; one who dies in the way of Allah, is a martyr; one who dies of plague is a martyr; one who dies of cholera is a martyr. Ibn Miqsam said: I testify the truth of your father's statement (with regard to this tradition) that the Prophet ﷺ said: One who is drowned is a martyr. (Using translation from Muslim 1915a)"
"3187","I testify regarding your father that he also narrated these words in the hadith: (The one who drowns) and dies is a martyr."
"3188","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""There are five types of martyrs: the one who dies of a stomach illness, the one who dies of plague, the one who drowns, the one who dies under debris, and the one who is martyred in the way of Allah (killed during battle)."
"3189","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to visit Abdullah ibn Thabit who was ill. He found that he was dominated (by the divine decree). The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called him loudly, but he did not respond. He uttered the Qur'anic verse ""We belong to Allah and to Him do we return"" and he said: We have been dominated against you, AburRabi'. Then the women cried and wept, and Ibn Atik began to silence them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Leave them, when the divine decree is made, no woman should weep. They (the people) asked: What is necessary happening, Messenger of Allah? He replied: Death. His daughter said: I hope you will be a martyr, for you have completed your preparations for jihad. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Allah Most High gave him a reward according to his intentions. What do you consider martyrdom? They said: Being killed in the cause of Allah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: There are seven types of martyrdom in addition to being killed in Allah's cause: one who dies of plague is a martyr; one who is drowned is a martyr; one who dies of pleurisy is a martyr; one who dies of an internal complaint is a martyr; one who is burnt to death is a martyr; who one is killed by a building falling on him is a martyr; and a woman who dies while pregnant is a martyr. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3111)"
"3190","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to visit Abdullah ibn Thabit who was ill. He found that he was dominated (by the divine decree). The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called him loudly, but he did not respond. He uttered the Qur'anic verse ""We belong to Allah and to Him do we return"" and he said: We have been dominated against you, AburRabi'. Then the women cried and wept, and Ibn Atik began to silence them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Leave them, when the divine decree is made, no woman should weep. They (the people) asked: What is necessary happening, Messenger of Allah? He replied: Death. His daughter said: I hope you will be a martyr, for you have completed your preparations for jihad. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Allah Most High gave him a reward according to his intentions. What do you consider martyrdom? They said: Being killed in the cause of Allah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: There are seven types of martyrdom in addition to being killed in Allah's cause: one who dies of plague is a martyr; one who is drowned is a martyr; one who dies of pleurisy is a martyr; one who dies of an internal complaint is a martyr; one who is burnt to death is a martyr; who one is killed by a building falling on him is a martyr; and a woman who dies while pregnant is a martyr. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3111)"
"3191","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever is wounded in the way of Allah, when he comes on the Day of Resurrection, its fragrance will be like the fragrance of musk and its color will be like the color of saffron. Upon it will be the seal of the martyrs. And whoever sincerely asks Allah Almighty for martyrdom, Allah Almighty grants him the reward of a martyr, even if that person dies on his bed.”"
"3192","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: If anyone asks Allah for martyrdom sincerely, Allah will make him reach the ranks of martyrs even if he died on his bed. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1520)"
"3193","The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, replied: This much. He said: So-and-so has wronged me; he has collected such and such amount from me. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: What will be the situation when rulers are imposed upon you who will wrong you even more than this? The people became worried at this. One of them said: O Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him! What will become of us at that time, when a person is not present among his camels, or animals, or in his field, or in his garden, and he pays the zakat on his wealth, yet he is wronged? O Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him! What should he do? The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Whoever pays the zakat on his wealth willingly, seeking the pleasure of Allah Almighty and the reward of the Hereafter, and does not withhold anything from it, and establishes prayer and pays zakat, and then he is wronged, then he should take up his weapon, and if he is killed while fighting, he will be a martyr. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:): The meaning of this narration is: When, in the collection of zakat or in any similar situation, a person is wronged, and there are Muslims with him who support him in this matter, and sufficiency is present, and their intention is not to gain worldly benefit. This does not mean that a person should throw himself into destruction, because the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said to Sayyiduna Abu Dharr al-Ghifari, may Allah be pleased with him: ""You should act with obedience and submission, even if the ruler is an Abyssinian (black) slave with a cut nose and ears."" And the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, also said: ""Whoever raises a weapon against us has nothing to do with us."
"3194","“Whoever is killed defending his property, he is a martyr.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2580)"
"3195","The narrator named Mu'ammar states: This hadith has reached us from Zuhri, in which these words are present: The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever is killed while protecting his wealth is a martyr."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:): This narration has been transmitted by the trustworthy and precise students of Zuhri, and all of them agree on narrating this hadith from Zuhri, from Talhah bin Abdullah, from Sayyiduna Sa'id bin Zayd (may Allah be pleased with him). Only Mu'ammar has differed; he mentioned a narrator named Abdur Rahman bin Sahl between Talhah bin Ubaidullah and Sayyiduna Sa'id bin Zayd (may Allah be pleased with him). I fear that he may have been mistaken in this matter, because Mu'ammar has narrated these words in this narration, which he received from Zuhri, so it is possible that he heard this narration from one of Zuhri's students. Therefore, the mind inclines more towards the other narrators."
"3196","The Prophet (peace be upon him) gave me permission, so Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Be mindful of what you recite. (So I began reciting:) “By Allah! If it were not for Allah, we would not have been guided, nor would we have given charity, nor would we have prayed. (O Allah), send down tranquility upon us, and if we face the enemy, make us steadfast. The polytheists have confronted us.” When I completed my rajaz, the Prophet (peace be upon him) asked: Who composed these verses? I replied: My brother did. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy on him. I said: O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! Some people did not perform his funeral prayer; they say: This person died by his own weapon. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: He is a person who died as a mujahid while striving in jihad."
"3197","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined two persons from among the martyrs of Uhud (in one garment), and said: Which of the two has learnt the Qur'an more ? When one of them was pointed to him, he advanced him in the grave, saying: I shall be witness to all these (martyrs) on the Day of Judgement. He then ordered them to be buried without being washed. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3138)"
"3198","I shall be present there (at the Cistern) before you. I shall be your witness and, by Allah, I perceive as if I am seeing with my own eyes my Cistern at this very state and I have been given the keys of the treasures of the earth or the keys of the earth and, by Allah, I am not afraid concerning you that you would associate anything (with Allah after me), but I am afraid that you would be vying with one another (for the possession of) the treasures of the earth. (Using translation from Muslim 2296a)"
"3199","I will precede you and I will be a witness for you. By Allah! I do not fear that you will commit shirk after me, but last night the keys to the treasures of the earth and the heavens were given to me, so I fear that you will become inclined towards the world. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) went into the house, and after that, he did not come out of the house until Allah took his (blessed soul). (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) specifically mentioned the martyrs, those who were martyred in battle, that he did not offer their funeral prayer. In this matter, he differentiated between them and other deceased persons, because all other deceased are given ghusl (ritual washing) and their funeral prayer is offered, but those who are martyred during battle, neither is their funeral prayer offered nor are they given ghusl; they are buried in their blood. As for the narration transmitted by Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) went and offered the funeral prayer for the martyrs of Uhud, this does not contradict the narration transmitted by Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), which we have already mentioned, because the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) went to Uhud and later prayed for the martyrs of Uhud, just as he used to pray for other deceased during the funeral prayer. The Arabs also use the word ""salat"" for supplication (dua). The Prophet’s (peace and blessings be upon him) going to the martyrs of Uhud, visiting them, and praying for them is a Sunnah for his Ummah after him, that they visit the martyrs of Uhud and pray for them, just as supplication is made for the deceased during the funeral prayer. Similarly, regarding the narration transmitted from Sayyiduna Zayd bin Abu Anisah (may Allah be pleased with him), which we have already mentioned, that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) went inside and after that did not come out of his house until Allah took his (blessed soul), this is a clear statement that the prayer was actually a supplication which the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) made specifically for those individuals, because the time of the Prophet’s (peace and blessings be upon him) departure from this world was near. If, in the narration transmitted from Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amir (may Allah be pleased with him), the word ""salat"" meant the funeral prayer like that of other deceased, then it would be necessary for the one who holds this view to accept that offering the funeral prayer at the grave is permissible, even if it is done seven years later, because the Battle of Uhud took place in the third year of Hijrah. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) went to pray for those individuals when the time of his departure from this world was near. So this happened seven years after the Battle of Uhud. Therefore, whoever argues from this narration that it is not permissible to offer the funeral prayer at the grave after seven years, it will be proven from this that this ""salat"" was actually a supplication for the deceased, not the funeral prayer, even if this is against the position of the one who claims that the hadith scholars transmit narrations which they do not understand, and they mention things which they do not comprehend, and transmit contradictory narrations."
"3200","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed prayer inside the Ka'bah, and soon there will come a person who will prohibit this. (The narrator says) Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) was sitting beside him at that time."
"3201","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) offered prayer inside the Ka'bah between two pillars."
"3202","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the Ka’bah on the Day of the Conquest (of Makkah), with Bilal and ‘Uthman bin Shaibah, and they locked the door behind them from the inside. When they came out, I asked Bilal: ‘Where did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray?’ He told me that when he entered, he turned to his right and prayed in the direction that he was facing, between the two columns.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3063)"
"3203","Messenger of Allah, ﷺ entered the House, and Usama, Bilal and Uthman b. Talha were with him, and they kept the door closed for a considerable time. Then it was opened and I was the first to enter the House and meet Bilal, and I said: Where did Messenger of Allah ﷺ observe prayer? He said: Between these two front pillars. I, however, forgot to ask him the number of rak'ahs that he observed. (Using translation from Muslim 1329d)"
"3204","‘Abd Allaah bin Umar said “The Apostle of Allaah ﷺ entered the Ka’bah and along with him entered Usamah bin Zaid, Uthman bin Talhah Al Hajabi and Bilal. He then closed the door and stayed there. ‘Abd Allah bin ‘Umar said “I asked Bilal when he came out What did the Apostle of Allaah ﷺ do (there)? He replied “He stood with a pillar on his left, two pillars on his right, and three pillars behind him. At that time the House (the Ka’bah) stood on six pillars. He then prayed. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2023)"
"3205","narration from Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyiduna Usamah bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with them both), because both of them were present with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) in the Ka’bah. So, once he narrated this report on the authority of Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him), and another time he narrated it on the authority of Sayyiduna Usamah bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with them both), so both chains are preserved."
"3206","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to perform prayer while there was a distance of three hand spans between him and the Qiblah."
"3207","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) entered the Ka'bah. There were six pillars inside it. The Prophet (peace be upon him) stood by each pillar and supplicated. There, the Prophet (peace be upon him) did not perform prayer."
"3208","The Qiblah is this direction, so face it and perform prayer. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:): Our Imams have interpreted these two narrations that the statements mentioned in both should be understood as negation and affirmation. These scholars have stated that Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) affirmed that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) performed prayer inside the Ka'bah, and Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) negated it, so the command to affirm something overrides the one who negates it. And in the incident of Uhud, it is incumbent upon us that Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) negated the performance of funeral prayer and washing of the martyrs on that day, and in my view, it is more appropriate that a distinction be made between the two narrations, that the actions mentioned in both be attributed to two different situations, and it be said that when the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) conquered Makkah and entered the Ka'bah, he performed prayer in it, as the students of Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) have narrated from Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) and Usama bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with them both), and this was on the day of the conquest of Makkah, as mentioned by Hassan bin Atiyyah from Nafi' from Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both). Whereas the negation by Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) performing prayer should be attributed to the situation where he says that Usama bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with them both) informed him about this, while Abu Sha'tha has narrated from Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) performed prayer inside the Ka'bah, and he says that Usama bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with them both) informed him about this. So when this narration is attributed to the situation we have mentioned, which refers to two different occasions, then the contradiction between them will be resolved, and each can be attributed to its specific situation."
"3209","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Spend without counting, otherwise Allah the Exalted will also give to you by counting, and do not tie the mouth of (your money pouch), otherwise Allah the Exalted will also tie the mouth (of your money pouch) when giving to you."
"3210","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Amr! The best wealth is the righteous wealth that is in the possession of a righteous man."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The narrator named Ali bin Rabah heard this narration from Amr bin Al-Aas (may Allah be pleased with him), and he heard this narration from Abu Qais on the authority of Sayyiduna Amr (may Allah be pleased with him); both of these chains are preserved."
"3211","I did so, then I presented myself before the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and I found him performing ablution. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) raised his head and looked me up and down. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Amr! I want to send you on a mission. May Allah keep you safe and grant you spoils of war, and I will also give you a share from the spoils."" The narrator says: I said, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! I did not accept Islam out of interest in wealth; rather, I accepted Islam to participate in jihad and to be with you."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Amr! Wealth is very good when it is pure and in the hands of a righteous man."
"3212","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Bring it to me. It was seven or five (uqiyah). I brought it and placed it in the palm of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). Then he said: What would Muhammad think of Allah if he were to meet Allah in such a state that this (gold) is with him? You should spend it."
"3213","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) instructed me to spend them, but due to the illness of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), I could not do so, until Allah Almighty improved his health. Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) inquired about them from me, so I replied: No, by Allah! Due to your illness, I could not spend them. Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had them brought and placed them on his palm, then he said: What would the Prophet of Allah think if he were to appear before Allah in such a state that these were still with him?"
"3214","I heard Sayyiduna Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying this: ""I do not like that I should have gold equal to the mountain of Uhud with me, and then after three days, even a single dinar remains with me, except that which I have kept aside for the repayment of a debt."
"3215","narrates this saying of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him): Indeed, the world is lush and sweet. If we give something from it with our own pleasure and without the greed of the receiver, and there is no evil of the soul in it, then there will be blessing in that thing for the person. But if we give it without our own pleasure and the receiver's greed is also involved, then there will be no blessing in it for him."
"3216","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you pay the zakat of your wealth, you have fulfilled the obligatory duty upon you. And whoever gathers wealth in a forbidden manner and then gives it in charity, he will not receive its reward; rather, its burden will remain upon him."
"3217","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “(In terms of coming into the world) we are the last, but on the Day of Resurrection we will be the first. (In terms of wealth and riches in the world) those who have abundance (in the Hereafter, in terms of reward and recompense) will be of lesser status, except for the person who says to his right, to his left, behind him, in front of him, like this and like this, and spreads his garment (i.e., spends his wealth in the way of Allah).”"
"3218","“Wretched is the slave of the Dinar and the slave of the Dirham, and the slave of velvet and the slave of the Khamisah.* If he is given, he is pleased and if he is not given, he does not fulfill (his oath of allegiance).” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4135)"
"3219","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man's heart always remains young in two things: love of long life and wealth."
"3220","""I (once) asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ (for something) and he gave it to me. Then I asked him (again) and he gave it to me. Then I asked him (again) and he gave it to me. Then I asked him (again), so he gave it to me. Then he said: 'O Hakim! Indeed this wealth is green and sweet, so whoever takes it without asking for it, he will be blessed in it. And whoever takes it, insisting upon it, he will not be blessed in it. He is like the one who eats but does not get satisfied and contended. And the upper hand (giving) is better than the lower hand (receiving)."" So Hakim said: ""I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! By the One who sent you with the Truth! I shall not ask anyone for anything after you until I depart the world.'""So Abu Bakr used to call Hakim to give him something, but he refused to accept it. Then 'Umar called him to give to him, but he refused to accept it. So 'Umar said: ""O you Muslims! I would like you to bear witness that I presented Hakim with his due of these spoils of war but he refused to accept it."" So Hakim never asked anyone of the people for anything after the Messenger of Allah, until he died. (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2463)"
"3221","The world is sweet and green (alluring) and verily Allah is going to install you as vicegerent in it in order to see how you act. So avoid the allurement of women: verily, the first trial for the people of Isra'il was caused by women. And in the hadith transmitted on the authority of Ibn Bashshar the words are:"" So that He should see how you act."" (Using translation from Muslim 2742)"
"3222","I do not fear poverty for you after me, rather I fear abundance (of wealth and riches) for you. And I do not fear (sins) committed by mistake for you, rather I fear (sins) committed deliberately by you."
"3223","""Indeed there is a fitnah for every Ummah, and the Fitnah for my Ummah is wealth."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2336)"
"3224","I will precede you and I will be a witness over you, and at this moment I am standing at my place and looking at my Hawd (cistern). By Allah! I do not fear that you will commit shirk after me, but I have been shown that the keys to the treasures of the earth have been given to me, so I fear regarding you that you will become inclined towards the world."
"3225","The Prophet’s Fear for His Ummah of the ..."
"3226","The Prophet’s Fear for His Ummah of the ..."
"3227","""The Messenger of Allah sat on the Minbar, and we sat around him. He said: 'What I fear most for you after I am gone is the (worldly) delights that will come to you.' And he spoke of this world and its attractions. A man said: 'Can good bring forth evil? 'The Messenger of Allah remained silent and it was said to him (that man): 'What is the matter with you? You speak to the Messenger of Allah when he does not speak to you? We noticed that he was receiving Revelation. Then he recovered and wiped off his sweat and said: I know what the questioner meant: he means that good never brings forth evil. But some of that which grows in the spring kills the animals or makes them sick, unless they eat Al-Khadir (kind of plant): if they eat their fill or it then turn to face the sun and then defecate and urinate and start to graze again. This wealth is fresh and sweet. Blessed is the wealth of a Muslim from which he gives to a Muslim from which he gives to orphans, the poor and wayfarers. The one who takes it unlawfully is like the one who eats but is never satisfied, and who eats but is never satisfied, and it will be a witness against him on the Day of Resurrection.""' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2581)"
"3228","""Two wolves free among sheep are no more destructive to them than a man's desire for wealth and honor is to his religion."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2376)"
"3229","""The Son Of Adan grows old, but two things keep him young: Desire for life and desire for wealth."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2339)"
"3230","I am also among those people."
"3231","I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) say: ""If a man were to possess a valley full of wealth, he would wish to have another like it. Nothing fills the belly of man except dust, and whoever repents, Allah accepts his repentance."
"3232","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If a man possesses two valleys of date palms, he will desire a third. Nothing fi"
"3233","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) say: \""If a man possesses a valley full of date-palm gardens, he would wish for another like it, and nothing will fill the belly of man except dust.\"" Only Umar bin Saeed has narrated this from Ahmad bin Abu Shu'aib, and among the narrators, A'mash is unique in narrating it with the wording of date-palm gardens; this has been stated by the Sheikh."""
"3234","I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""If a man possesses a valley of wealth, he will wish that he had another like it. Nothing fills the belly of man except dust, and Allah accepts the repentance of whoever repents."
"3235","If there were two valleys of gold for the son of Adam, he would long for another one. and his mouth will not be filled but with dust, and Allah returns to him who repents. (Using translation from Muslim 1048c)"
"3236","If the son of Adam were to possess two valleys of riches. he would long for the third one. And the stomach of the son of Adam is not filled but with dust. And Allah returns to him who repents. (Using translation from Muslim 1048a)"
"3237","I said: Allah and His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) have spoken the truth: If a man has two valleys of gold, he will desire a third with them. Only dust can fill the belly of man, and whoever repents, Allah accepts his repentance. The narrator says: Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) asked me: What do you say? The narrator says: I replied: Sayyiduna Ubayy bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to me in the same way. So Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Get up and come with me to him. The narrator says: Then Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) came to him and asked: What did he narrate? So Sayyiduna Ubayy (may Allah be pleased with him) informed: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me in the same way."
"3238","narrates from Sayyiduna Abu Darda’ (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Sustenance seeks out a servant just as death seeks him out.”"
"3239","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Do not hasten towards sustenance, for a servant does not die until the last portion of his allotted sustenance reaches him. And in seeking it, be mindful to acquire what is lawful and leave what is unlawful."
"3240","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Take it, if you had not come to it, it would have come to you."
"3241","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Do not hasten towards sustenance, for a servant does not die until the last portion of his allotted sustenance reaches him. Seek what is lawful and abandon what is unlawful."
"3242","narrate: We presented ourselves before the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) while he was engaged in some construction. When he finished, he called us and said: Do not incline towards sustenance (rizq) in such a way that your heads begin to spin (or as long as your head spins, meaning as long as you are alive, do not remain completely preoccupied with sustenance), because when a person is born from his mother, he is red in color and does not even have skin over him, yet Allah Almighty grants him and provides him with sustenance."
"3243","narration is: When a person spends something on the earth which is beyond his basic needs, he will not be rewarded for it."
"3244","A servant says, My wealth. my wealth, but out of his wealth three things are only his: whatever he eats and makes use of or by means of which he dresses himself and it wears out or he gives as charity, and this is what he stored for himself (as a reward for the Hereafter), and what is beyond this (it is of no use to you) because you are to depart and leave it for other people. (Using translation from Muslim 2959a)"
"3245","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Worship Allah, do not associate anyone with Him, establish prayer, pay zakat, maintain ties of kinship, and now let her go. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) meant: let the she-camel go."
"3246","A man said, ""O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! Inform me of a deed which will make me enter Paradise."" The people said, ""What is the matter with him? What is the matter with him?"" Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""He has something to ask (what he needs greatly)."" The Prophet ﷺ said (to him), (In order to enter Paradise) you should worship Allah and join none in worship with Him: You should offer prayers perfectly, give obligatory charity (Zakat), and keep good relations with your Kith and kin."" He then said, ""Leave it!"" (The sub-narrator said, ""It seems that the Prophet ﷺ was riding his she camel."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 5983)"
"3247","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever worships Allah and does not associate anyone with Him, establishes prayer, pays zakat, fasts in Ramadan, and avoids major sins, he will enter Paradise."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) Salman Aghar has two sons, one is Abdullah and the other is Ubaidullah, and both have narrated this hadith from their father; here, its narrator is Abdullah."
"3248","Charity does not decrease wealth, no one forgives another except that Allah increases his honor, and no one humbles himself for the sake of Allah except that Allah raises his status. (Using translation from Muslim 2588)"
"3249","Abu Sa’id Al Khudri said “A Bedouin asked the Prophet ﷺ about emigration. He replied “Woe to you! The matter of emigration is severe. Have you a Camel? He said, Yes. He asked “Do you pay its zakat? He said, Yes. He said, Then work (anywhere) beyond the seas. Allaah will not reduce anything from (the reward of) your work. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2477)"
"3250","I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: What is evil in a man are alarming niggardliness and unrestrained cowardice. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2511)"
"3251","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The dust in the cause of Allah and the smoke of Hell will never be combined in the lungs of a slave, and the stinginess and faith can never be combined in a slave's heart."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3110)"
"3252","""The one who consumes Riba, the one who pays it, and the one who writes it down, if they know that it is Riba; the woman who does tattoos and the woman who has that done for the purpose of beautification; the one who withholds Sadaqah (Zakah); and the one who reverts to the life of a Bedouin after having emigrated- they will (all) be cursed upon the tongue of Muhammad [SAW] on the Day of Resurrection."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5102)"
"3253","No owner of the treasure who does not pay Zakat (would be spared) but (his hoards) would be heated in the Fire of Hell and these would be made into plates and with these his sides, his forehead would be cauterised till Allah would pronounce judgment among His servants during a day, the extent of which would be fifty thousand years. He would then see his path, leading either to Paradise or to Hell. And no owner of the camels who does not pay Zakat (would be spared) but a soft sandy plain would be set for him and they (the camels) would be made to pass over him till the last of them would be made to return till Allah would pronounce judgment among His servants during a day the extent of which would be fifty thousand years. He would then see his path leading him to Paradise or leading him to Hell. And no owner of the (cattle and) goats who does not pay Zakat (would be spared) but a soft sandy plain would be set for him, he would find none of them missing, with twisted horns, without horns, or with broken horns, and they will gore him with their horns and trample him with their hoofs and they would be made to pass over him till the last of them would be made to return till Allah would pronounce judgment among His servants, during a day the extent of which would be fifty thousand years, and he would see the paths leading to Paradise or to Hell. Suhail said: I do not know whether he made mention of the cows. They said: Messenger of Allah ﷺ, what about the horses? He said: The horses have goodness in their foreheads (or he said) or goodness is ingrained in the foreheads of the horses (Suhail said: I am in doubt as to what was actually said) up till the Day of judgement. The horses are of three kinds. They are a source of reward to a person, they are a covering to a person, and they are a burden to a person. As for those which bring reward is that a person would get reward who rears them for the sake of Allah and trains them for Him, and nothing disappears in their stomachs but Allah would record for him a good deed. And if they were to graze in the meadow, they would eat nothing but Allah would record for him a reward. And if they were to drink water from the canal, with every drop that, would disappear in their stomachs there would be reward (for the owner). He went on describing till a reward was mentioned for their urine and dung. And if they pranced a course or two, there would be recorded a reward for every pace that they covered. As for one for whom they are a covering, he is the man who rears them for honour and dignity but does not forget the right of their backs and their stomachs, in plenty and adversity, As regards one for whom they are a burden, he is that who rears them for vainglory and showing off to the people; for him they are, the burden. They said: Messenger of Allah, what about asses? He said: Allah has not revealed to me anything in regards to it except this one comprehensive verse:"" He who does an atom's weight of good will see it, and he who does an atom's weight of evil will see it"" (xcix. 7). (Using translation from Muslim 987c)"
"3254","I have to do with you?' The treasure will say, 'I am your treasure, I am your treasure.' Then its owner will stretch out his hand towards it, and it will bite his hand."
"3255","I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Whoever owns camels and does not do good regarding them (i.e., does not pay their zakat), then on the Day of Resurrection, they will come healthier than before. That person will be made to sit in an open field before them, and they will trample him with their legs and feet. Whoever owns cows (and does not pay their zakat), then those cows will come on the Day of Resurrection healthier than before. That person will be made to sit in an open field before them, and they will gore him with their horns and trample him with their feet. There will not be any cow among them without horns or with broken horns. Whoever owns a treasure (and does not pay its zakat), then that treasure will come on the Day of Resurrection in the form of a bald-headed snake and will open its mouth and chase after him. When it comes near him, he will try to run away from it, but his Lord will call out to him: 'This is your treasure, which you kept stored up.' When that person sees that he cannot escape from it, he will stretch out his hand towards its mouth, and the snake will chew his hand just as a camel chews something."
"3256","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, whoever dies leaving behind camels, cows, or goats for which he did not pay zakat, then on the Day of Resurrection they will be resurrected in a form larger and heavier than before. They will gore him with their horns and trample him with their hooves. When the last of them passes by, the first will return, and this will continue until Allah Almighty judges between the people."
"3257","I am your treasure which you left behind.' Then that treasure will keep following him until the person stretches out his hand towards it, and the treasure will chew his hand and then swallow his entire being."
"3258","The treasure of one of you will come on the Day of Resurrection in the form of a bald snake. It will follow its owner, and the owner will try to escape from it, but it will keep following him, until he puts his fingers into its mouth."
"3259","I came to Medina and when I was in the company of the grandees of Quraish a man with a crude body and an uncouth face wearing coarse clothes came there. He stood up before them and said: Give glad tidings to those whom who amass riches of the stones which would be heated in the Fire of Hell, and would be placed at the tick of the chest till it would project from the shoulder bone and would he put on the shoulder bone till it would project from the tick of his chest, and it (this stone) would continue passing and repassing (from one side to the other). He (the narrator) said: Then people hung their heads and I saw none among them giving any answer. He then returned and I followed him till he sat near a pillar. I said: I find that these (people) disliked what you said to them and they do not understand anything. My friend Abu'l-Qasim (Muhammad) (may peace he upon him) called me and I responded to him, and he said: Do you see Uhud? I saw the sun (shining) on me and I thought that he would send me on an errand for him. So I said: I see it. Upon this he said: Nothing would delight me more than this that I should have gold like it (equal to the bulk of Uhud), and I should spend it all except three dinars. (How sad it is) that they hoard worldly riches, and they know nothing. I said: What about you and your brothers Quraish? You do not go to thein for any need and do not accept anything from them. He said: By Allah, I neither beg anything from them (from worldly goods), nor do I ask them anything about religion till I meet my Allah and His Messenger. (Using translation from Muslim 992a)"
"3260","While I was in the company of the (elites) of Quraiah, Abu Dharr came there and he was saying: Give glad tidings to the hoarders of riches that their backs would be branded (so deeply) that (the hot Iron) would come out of their sides, and when the backs of their necks would be branded, it would come out of their foreheads. He (Abu Dharr) then went away and sat down. I asked who he was. They said: He is Abu Dharr. I went to him and said to him: What is this that I heard from you which you were saying before? He said: I said nothing but only that which I heard from their Prophet ﷺ. I again said: What do you say about this gift? He said: Take it, for today it is a help. But when it becomes a price for your religion, then abandon it. (Using translation from Muslim 992b)"
"3261","I have to do with you?' It will say: 'I am your treasure.' Then it will bite his hand."",""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ  said"",""""""Wealth that is not given its due will come to its owner on the Day of Judgment in the form of a camel"","" trampling him with its hooves. Cattle and sheep will come to their owner"","" trampling him with their hooves and pushing him with their horns. A treasure"","" being bold and dark"","" will confront its owner who will run away from it. Then the owner will turn to it"","" yet again it will run away from him"","" saying: 'What is between me and you?' The owner will reply: 'I am your treasure!' The treasure will then devour his hand."""""""
"3262","A man from Najd with unkempt hair came to Messenger of Allah ﷺ and we heard his loud voice but could not understand what he was saying, till he came near and then we came to know that he was asking about Islam. Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""You have to offer prayers perfectly five times in a day and night (24 hours)."" The man asked, ""Is there any more (praying)?"" Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied, ""No, but if you want to offer the Nawafil prayers (you can)."" Messenger of Allah ﷺ further said to him: ""You have to observe fasts during the month of Ramadan."" The man asked, ""Is there any more fasting?"" Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied, ""No, but if you want to observe the Nawafil fasts (you can.)"" Then Messenger of Allah ﷺ further said to him, ""You have to pay the Zakat (obligatory charity)."" The man asked, ""Is there any thing other than the Zakat for me to pay?"" Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied, ""No, unless you want to give alms of your own."" And then that man retreated saying, ""By Allah! I will neither do less nor more than this."" Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""If what he said is true, then he will be successful (i.e. he will be granted Paradise)."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 46)"
"3263","The people mentioned this to the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), so he (peace be upon him) said: These two are marks of branding."
"3264","The people said: O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! Please perform the funeral prayer for him. The Prophet (peace be upon him) asked: Did he leave behind any debt? They replied: No. The Prophet (peace be upon him) asked: Did he leave behind anything? They replied: Three dinars. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Three things with which he will be branded. Another funeral was brought and the people said: O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), please perform the funeral prayer for him. The Prophet (peace be upon him) asked: Did he leave behind any debt? They replied: Yes. The Prophet (peace be upon him) asked: Did he leave behind anything? The people replied: No. One of the Ansar, whose name was Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him), said: O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! The repayment of his debt is my responsibility. The narrator says: So the Prophet (peace be upon him) performed his funeral prayer."
"3265","I give him. He asks me again, so I give him. This happens three times, then that person turns and leaves, even though he has put fire in his clothes, at the time when he is returning to his home."
"3266","These are the types of charity (zakah) that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made obligatory upon the Muslims and which Allah, may He be glorified and exalted, enjoined upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Whoever among the Muslims is asked to pay it in the proper manner, let him give it; whoever is asked for more than that, let him not give it. For less than twenty-five camels, for each five, one sheep (should be given). If the number reaches twenty-five, then one she-camel in its second year (should be given), up to thirty-five. If there is no she-camel in its second year, then a he-camel in its third year (may be given). If the number reaches thirty-six, then a she-camel in its third year (should be given), up to forty-five. If the number reaches forty-six, then a she-camel in its fourth year that has been bred to a stallion camel should be given, up to sixty, If the number reaches sixty-one, then a she-camel in its fifth year (should be given), up to seventy five. If the number reaches seventy-six, then two she-camels in their second year (should be given), up to ninety. If the number reaches ninety-one, then two she camels in their fourth year that have been bred to a stallion camel should be given, up to one hundred and twenty. If the number is more than one hundred and twenty, then for every forty camels, a she-camel limits third year should be given and for every fifty a she-camel in its fourth year. If the ages of the camels for zakah differ, if what is due is a she-camel in its fifth year but he does not own such a camel, but he has a she-camel in its fourth year, then that will be accepted from him and he should add to it two sheep, if available, or twenty dirhams. If what is due from him is a she-camel in its fourth year and he only has a she camel in its fifth year, it should be accepted from him and the zakat collector should give him back twenty dirhams or two sheep. If what is due from him is a shecamel in its fourth year, but he does not have such a cameland he has a she-camel in its third year, then it should be accepted from him and he should add to it two sheep, is available, or twenty dirhams. If what is due from him is a she camel in its second year, but he only has a he-camel in its third year, then it should be accepted from him and nothing should be added to it. If he has only four camels, no zakah is due unless the owner wants to give it. With regard to zakah on sheep in the pasture, if there are forty sheep, then one sheep is due as zakah, up to one hundred and twenty sheep. of there is one more than that, then two sheep are due, up to two hundred. If there is one more than that then three sheep are due, up to three hundred. If there is one more than that, then for every hundred sheep, one sheep is due No toothless or defective sheep should be taken as zakah and neither should a ram, unless the one who is giving allows that. Separate flocks should not be put together and flocks should not be divided so as to avoid or reduce zakah. If there are two partners [and the zakah-collector comes and takes zakah), they should settle the matter between them on a fair basis. If a man's flock is grazing if it is one less than forty, then no zakah is due on it unless the owner wants to give it. On silver the zakah is one quarter of one tenth; if the wealth is only one hundred and ninety dirhams, then no zakah is due on it unless the owner wants to give it. (Using translation from Aḥmad 72)"
"3267","""There is no 'bringing', no 'avoidance' and no Shighar in Islam, and whoever robs, he is not one of us."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3335)"
"3268","That the Apostle of Allaah ﷺ as saying No sadaqah(zakat) is payable on less than five camels, on less than five ounces of silver and on less than five camel loads(wasq). (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1558)"
"3269","I passed by a man from the tribe of Bali who had thirty (30) camels. I said to him: ""It is obligatory upon you to give a bint makhad (a young she-camel) from these camels."" He said: ""This is such an animal that cannot be ridden and does not give milk. I do not like to present inferior wealth to Allah. You have the choice (to take another animal)."" Sayyiduna Ubayy (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: ""I cannot take from you more than what is obligatory upon you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is present, so go to him."" That man went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said the same thing he had said to Sayyiduna Ubayy (may Allah be pleased with him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""This is what is obligatory upon you. If you bring more than this, we will accept it from you."" He said: ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! This is a fat, healthy she-camel. Who will take possession of it?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed, so a man took possession of it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed for blessing in that man's wealth. The narrator named 'Ammarah says: After that, a long time passed. Marwan (who was the governor of Madinah) sent me to collect zakat from the tribes of Bali and Udhrah. This was during the caliphate of Sayyiduna Amir Mu'awiyah (may Allah be pleased with him). I passed by that man, and according to my calculation, the zakat on his wealth was thirty (30) hiqqah, including one male animal, and the number of his camels was one thousand five hundred. Ibn Ishaq says: I asked the narrator named Abdullah bin Abu Bakr: ""What is meant by a male animal?"" He replied: ""The Sunnah is that when a person's zakat reaches thirty (30) hiqqah, then a male animal is also to be taken along with them."
"3270","I find it nor will I bring it. So the Prophet (peace be upon him) did not assign him this responsibility."
"3271","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying No sadaqah is due from a Muslim on his slave or his horse. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1595)"
"3272","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Zakat is not obligatory on a man's horse or slave, except that (for the slave) Sadaqat al-Fitr is obligatory."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:): This narration contains evidence that a slave does not own anything, because the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) made Sadaqat al-Fitr obligatory for the slave, but its payment is not obligatory upon him; rather, it is obligatory upon his owner."
"3273","The Prophet ﷺ sent Umar b. al-Khattab to collect sadaqa (All the people paid the zakat but ibn-jamil, Khalid b. al-walid and al-abbas refused. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said : Ibn-jamil is not (so much) objecting, but he was poor and Allah enriched him. As for Khalid b. Walid, you are wronging him, for he has kept back his courts of mail and weapons to use them in Allah’s path. As for al-Abbas, the uncle of the Messenger of Allah(May peace be upon him), I shall be responsible for it and an equal amount along with it. Then he said did you not know(Umar) that a man’s paternal uncle is of the same stock as the father or his father? (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1623)"
"3274","“Whenever a man brought Sadaqah to the Messenger of Allah, he would bless him. I brought him the Sadaqah of my wealth and he said: 'Allhumma, salli ala ali abi awfa(O Allah! Send blessing upon the family of Abu Awfa).' ” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1796)"
"3275","""No sadaqah is due on less than five Awaq, no Sadaqah is due on less than five Dhawd, no Sadaqah is due on less than five Awsuq."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2487)"
"3276","""No Zakah is due on wheat or dates unless the amount reaches five Awsuq. No Zakah is due on silver unless the amount reaches five Awaq. No Zakah is due on camels until the number reaches five Dhawd."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2484)"
"3277","That the Apostle of Allaah ﷺ as saying No sadaqah(zakat) is payable on less than five camels, on less than five ounces of silver and on less than five camel loads(wasq). (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1558)"
"3278","the Prophet used to send to the people one who would assess their vineyards and fruits. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1819)"
"3279","The estimation of the grapevine will be made just as the estimation of the date palm is made, and then its zakat will be paid in the form of grapes, just as the zakat of the date palm is paid in the form of dates.”"
"3280","Sayyiduna Sahl bin Abu Hathma (may Allah be pleased with him) came to our mosque and narrated this hadith to us that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you estimate the produce, then collect it and leave one third of it; if you do not leave one third, then leave one fourth."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:): This narration can have two meanings: one is that he leaves one third or one fourth from the 'ushr, and the second meaning is that before taking the 'ushr, he leaves it from the dates themselves, especially when the orchard is large."
"3281","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Zakat is not obligatory on silver until it reaches five awqiyah. Zakat is not obligatory on dates until they reach five wasq. Zakat is not obligatory on camels until they reach five camels."
"3282","That the Apostle of Allaah ﷺ as saying No sadaqah(zakat) is payable on less than five camels, on less than five ounces of silver and on less than five camel loads(wasq). (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1558)"
"3283","""The Messenger of Allah said: ""Volume is to be measured according to the system of the people of Al-Madinah, and weight is to be measured according to the system of the peole of Makkah.""' (Sahih) This is the wording of Ishaq (one of the narrators). (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4594)"
"3284","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""O Allah! Bless our sa’ for us, bless for us what is little and what is much, and grant us, along with this blessing, two more blessings."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The fact that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not object to their words when they said, ""Our sa’ is the smallest sa’,"" is a clear statement that the sa’ of the people of Madinah is the smallest among all sa’s. From the time of the Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) until our present era, there has been no disagreement among the scholars regarding this sa’ and its measurement, except for the difference of opinion between the people of Hijaz and the people of Iraq. The people of Hijaz say that one sa’ is five ratl and one third of a ratl, while the people of Iraq say that one sa’ is eight ratl. Thus, we do not find any disagreement among the scholars regarding the measurement of the sa’, except what we have mentioned. Therefore, it is authentically established that the sa’ of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was five ratl and one third of a ratl, because this is the smallest sa’, and the view of the one who claims that one sa’ is eight ratl is proven to be incorrect, as he has stated this without any evidence that can be considered authentic."
"3285","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying A tenth is payable on what is watered by rain or rivers or brooks or from underground moisture and a twentieth on what is watered by draught camels. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1596)"
"3286","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""That which is irrigated by rainfall or by rivers, and that which is 'ushri, one-tenth will be taken from it."
"3287","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying A tenth is payable on what is watered by rain or rivers or brooks or from underground moisture and a twentieth on what is watered by draught camels. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1596)"
"3288","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) had ordered regarding the mosque that a bunch (of fruit) from every garden should be placed in it. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:): This narrator named Abdullah is Abdullah bin Umar bin Hafs bin Asim bin Umar bin Khattab. He was among the devout worshippers of the people of Madinah. He was dominated by asceticism and worship, so he used to mix up narrations and would not realize it. Therefore, when a large number of such mistakes were found in the narrations transmitted by him, it became invalid to use his narrations as evidence. So, regarding this narration, our reliance will be on the narration transmitted by his brother Ubaidullah, not on him."
"3289","Jabir bin ‘Abdallah said The bProphet (SWAS) commanded that he who plucks ten wasqs of dates from date palms should hang a bunch of dates in the mosque for the poor (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1662)"
"3290","the Messenger of Allah said: “Charity is not permissible for a rich person, or for one who is strong and healthy. ” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1839)"
"3291","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ‘O Qabeesah, we take your payment upon ourselves and will pay it from the camels of charity.’ Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ‘(Asking for something) is only permissible for three types of people: one who takes responsibility for a payment, for him it is permissible to ask until he pays off that debt; one who is afflicted by a calamity that destroys his produce, for him it is permissible to ask until he fulfills his needs (the narrator is unsure about one word here); and one who is struck by hunger and three wise men from his tribe testify that it has become permissible for him to ask, then it is permissible for him to ask until he fulfills his basic needs. Other than this, asking is forbidden.’"
"3292","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates this statement of the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him: \""I return to my house and find a fallen date there. I pick it up to eat it, then I fear that it might be from charity, so I put it back.\"""""
"3293","Sayyiduna Abu Rafi’ (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): “Zakat is not lawful for us; the slave of any people is considered part of them.”"""
"3294","narrates: Dates of zakat were brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Sayyiduna Imam Hasan bin Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) picked up one of those dates. He put it in his mouth, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Spit it out, spit it out, zakat is not lawful for us."
"3295","Sayyiduna Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Sayyiduna Imam Hasan bin Ali"
